// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/course/fpga_course_v2.t27 -- the plan for version 2 of the t27.ai FPGA course,
// "From zero to a chip" (gHashTag/trinity apps/website/specs/course/course.t27), as data.
//
// AUDITED AT gHashTag/trinity origin/main ca7ec465e5, 2026-11-07: the 27 lesson texts and
// tasks, the page (src/pages/Course.tsx) and the generator (scripts/course-from-spec.mjs).
//
// HOW TO READ IT. WEAK_* is one row per weak point, sorted by score. A score is
// impact * 100 / cost, with impact and cost on 1..9. Both are judgements made during the
// audit, not measurements: no learner data exists for this course. The cut (CUT) is the
// first rows whose cost is at most a third of the total and whose impact is at least half;
// that is the Pareto set this version fixes first. TASK_* is the work, one row per task,
// each with its issue. A task's state changes only in a PR that also changes the work.
//
// CLAIMS. Before working a task, take `tri loop claim course-v2-<task id>` (exit 0 = yours,
// 1 = someone holds it). Set the row to CLAIMED in the same PR as the work, DONE after merge.
// TASK_PR names the PR that carries a task (0 = none yet), so any agent reading this file sees
// what is in progress and where; a DONE task always names one, an OPEN task never does.
//
// COMPETITORS, checked in a browser on 2026-11-07 (COMP_*): what each one does that this
// course does not yet do. Not a ranking of them.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: that version 2 teaches better than version 1. It removes checked falsehoods
// (W1) and states the learning law (W2, W4, W5); whether readers learn more is unmeasured.
// ASCII only (L3). phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module course_fpga_course_v2;

